SUMMARY:Early Modern Philosophy Research Interest Group (Patricia Sheridan\, Guelph)
DESCRIPTION:The Early Modern Philosophy Research Interest Group welcomes Patricia Sheridan\, an associate professor at the University of Guelph. She works on thinkers and issues in the early modern period (the 17th and 18th centuries). She is chiefly interested in early modern women philosophers\, John Locke\, and moral philosophy in the early modern period. She has recently been interested in the concept of virtue in Catharine Trotter Cockburn\, Anne Conway\, Damaris Masham\, Mary Astell\, as well as in John Locke. She is interested in tracing the development of the idea of virtue through the period as well as examining the role accorded to the passions\, in many early modern thinkers\, as forming the virtuous agent. \nTalk Title\nTBA \nTalk Abstract\nTBA
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/early-modern-philosophy-research-interest-group-patricia-sheridan-guelph/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building\, Room 418\, 170 St. George Street\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5R 2M8\, Canada
